{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1168201-small-question-about-the-elemental-blessing","id":1168201,"title":"Small question about the Elemental blessing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-16T09:19:03-08:00","id":1168201,"title":"Small question about the Elemental blessing","content":"So, each Seeming possesses a blessing that has what might be called an anti-Loophole, a condition under which the changeling must spend Glamour in order to benefit from it. It seems that the general idea behind these conditions is that the blessing is a reinforcement (by the Wyrd perhaps?) of a certain fairy-tale archetype, and it is only by spending Glamour that a changeling can cheat the system and act out of character, so to speak: the Ogre breaking kneecaps for his own sake, or the Wizened caught without the tools of her trade, etc.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm not sure what to make of the Elemental's Seeming blessing. From the manuscript preview: &quot;This ability costs a point of Glamour per action if he has fewer than half his maximum Willpower points remaining.&quot; Is this meant to represent the Torrent's freedom-loving nature, and that lacking Willpower draws one closer to bending to the desires of others? Is it because Sprites are assumed to always be acting at full strength (i.e., spending Willpower on rolls) in everything they do?<br /> <br /> Any other perspectives on this matter would be appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T15:15:01-08:00","id":1168257,"title":"","content":"My guess when under half willpower, the glamour makes up for lost drive. <br /> <br /> Or it's simply part of the deal the Wizened have with the Wyrd, for unknowable reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T21:43:49-08:00","id":1168306,"title":"","content":"A character who does not want for Willpower is anchored, their reserves of will unflagging and their selfhood not overly dependent upon the principles and peccadilloes that renew them in the lean times.<br /> <br /> A Torrent who cannot make a decent claim at occupying this state is cut off from himself, his world-nature ragged and unrefined; his natural command of his surroundings falters in this state, and he must rely instead upon the common currency of the fae to fill the gap.<br /> <br /> Put more simply, an Elemental struggles with the purity of their own agency, and while part of that identity struggle is bound up in Clarity, Willpower serves a similar purpose without giving one of the Resistance-boosting seemings a paradoxically fragile blessing and has a lot more broad-scope systems that can mess with it at any given point along the continuum of gameplay.<br /> <br /> (Note how badly that e.g. the Competitive Condition can fuck up a Sprite who relies on their blessing a lot. Note also that this means Torrents in their element have more incentive to play to their Needle and Thread.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-16T22:02:02-08:00","id":1168310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1168201-small-question-about-the-elemental-blessing#post1168201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm not sure what to make of the Elemental's Seeming blessing. From the manuscript preview: &quot;This ability costs a point of Glamour per action if he has fewer than half his maximum Willpower points remaining.&quot; Is this meant to represent the Torrent's freedom-loving nature, and that lacking Willpower draws one closer to bending to the desires of others? Is it because Sprites are assumed to always be acting at full strength (i.e., spending Willpower on rolls) in everything they do?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you interpreting this passage as saying that you need to be under half Willpower to perform the ability, possibly? If so, that might be the disconnect. You can do it over half Willpower for free, or do it under half Willpower by spending Glamour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-17T07:21:25-08:00","id":1168366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1168201-small-question-about-the-elemental-blessing?p=1168306#post1168306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A character who does not want for Willpower is anchored, their reserves of will unflagging and their selfhood not overly dependent upon the principles and peccadilloes that renew them in the lean times.<br /> <br /> A Torrent who cannot make a decent claim at occupying this state is cut off from himself, his world-nature ragged and unrefined; his natural command of his surroundings falters in this state, and he must rely instead upon the common currency of the fae to fill the gap.<br /> <br /> Put more simply, an Elemental struggles with the purity of their own agency, and while part of that identity struggle is bound up in Clarity, Willpower serves a similar purpose without giving one of the Resistance-boosting seemings a paradoxically fragile blessing and has a lot more broad-scope systems that can mess with it at any given point along the continuum of gameplay.<br /> <br /> (Note how badly that e.g. the Competitive Condition can fuck up a Sprite who relies on their blessing a lot. Note also that this means Torrents in their element have more incentive to play to their Needle and Thread.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This interpretation is intriguing. I like it. I guess it also ties together the Elemental's two expendable resources, since if your Glamour is low you'll want to preserve Willpower too if you think your Blessing will be useful in the scene, which becomes even more of a predicament if someone is trying to coerce you and you really don't want to deal with a Clarity attack at the moment. And then once you start picking up Frailties. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}